{"name":"Aloof Lama","hex":"#d6c5a0","fetched":"2026-10-21","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aloof","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["At or from a distance, but within view, or at a small distance; apart; away.","Without sympathy; unfavorably."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Either physically or emotionally remote: distant, standoffish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aloof"},{"term":"lama","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A master of Tibetan Buddhism."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of llama."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lama"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lama","blocks":[{"text":"Lama is a title bestowed to a realized practitioner of the Dharma in Tibetan Buddhism. Not all monks are lamas, while nuns and female practitioners can be recognized and entitled as lamas. The Tibetan word la-ma means \"high mother\", and reflects the qualities of the person who is called a lama."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tibetian_Wheel.svg/330px-Tibetian_Wheel.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lama","wikidata":"Q191421"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"aloof":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/12/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-aloof.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/1/12/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-aloof.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-aloof.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/1/12/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-aloof.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-aloof.wav.ogg"}],"lama":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5a/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-llama.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=origin